comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T21:22:55.185Z","harness:codex","Start evidence 2026-08-10: reused canonical assertion item after all-status duplicate search. This tranche implements assertion declaration validation and evaluation on the measurement substrate, including mandatory proven controls and explicit lifecycle/enforcement semantics."
  "2026-08-10T23:01:03.730Z","harness:codex","Completion evidence 2026-08-11: assertions now require exactly one polarity, explicit all/active/filter scope, hold-or-reasoned-retire lifetime, enforcement level, owner linkage, and a proven negative control. Evaluation reports population and observed/bound data; monotone tightening is automatic, while weakening is refused unless a live linked Decision authorizes it. Unit and action tests passed inside the 7,201-test exact-coverage run and the packed CLI acceptance exercised a passing assertion end to end."
  "2026-08-10T23:31:46.619Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review work 2026-08-11 Europe/Vienna (PM event timestamps remain UTC): actively removing synthesized Decision authorization, completing measurement-reference integrity, signed-bound coverage, and negative-control proof."
  "2026-08-11T00:55:42.604Z","harness:codex","Exact-head completion evidence 2026-08-11: weakening now accepts only an explicitly named terminal Decision item, never a synthesized or arbitrary Decision; filter and derived measurement references participate in the same integrity checks; signed finite assertion bounds and a numeric negative control are covered. Focused action/assertion tests and the exact 100/100/100/100 suite passed."
  "2026-08-11T02:02:16.297Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review completion 2026-08-11: the strict transport schema now requires a non-empty retire_reason exactly when lifetime is retire, matching runtime assertion validation; full-contract regression coverage and the exact suite passed."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T23:01:04.318Z","harness:codex","A weakening authorization must be resolved against the live workspace item graph, not accepted as a caller string; this keeps a Decision auditable and prevents transport-specific policy bypasses."
  "2026-08-11T00:55:43.154Z","harness:codex","Authorization is provenance, not type presence: a weakening must name exactly one terminal Decision so replay can prove which decision granted the exception."
